    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# RAG Workflow for Knowledge Base - Update\n\n## Purpose\nKeeps the Pinecone vector store consistent with edits to existing knowledge-base files. When a KB document is modified in Drive (or programmatically by another workflow), this pipeline removes the old vectors and re-embeds the latest content so retrieval never serves stale answers.\n\n## How it works\n- Two entry points: a Google Drive trigger that watches the Knowledge_Base folder for file updates, and an Execute-Workflow trigger that accepts `fileId` + `fileName` from other workflows\n- Normalizes input fields, then deletes all existing Pinecone vectors for the file via a metadata-filter HTTP request to the Pinecone API\n- Downloads the latest file binary from Drive, attaches fresh metadata (fileId, fileName, uploadDate)\n- Re-splits and re-embeds the document with OpenAI embeddings and inserts the new chunks into the Pinecone `company-files` index\n- Upserts the tracker row in Rag_File_Tracker (status = updated) and forwards to the PageIndex update sub-workflow\n\n## Triggered by\n- Google Drive trigger on the `Knowledge_Base` folder (fileUpdated, polled every minute)\n- Execute Workflow trigger with `fileId` + `fileName` (called by other workflows)\n\n## Calls (sub-workflows)\n- PageIndex Workflow for Knowledge Base - Update  refreshes the same document in PageIndex after the Pinecone re-embed succeeds.\n\n## Reads/writes\n- Reads from Google Drive `Knowledge_Base` folder\n- Deletes from and writes to Pinecone index `company-files` (with OpenAI embeddings)\n- Upserts Google Sheets `Customer_Support_Data`  `Rag_File_Tracker`",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 1100,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky-overview-doc",
      "name": "Workflow Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1200,
        -400
      ]
    }
